@*
    WizardSection — shared numbered-card primitive for the six wizards.
    M.2d.1 deliverable per the v2 plan §5.2 (round-1 #2 — the most useful
    missing primitive surfaced in ChatGPT review).

    Responsibilities (chrome only):
      * MudPaper wrapper with consistent elevation + padding + margin.
      * Numbered title — "{Index}. {Title}".
      * Optional description text rendered as a caption.
      * ChildContent slot — the section body.

    What this is NOT responsible for (anti-coupling lock — round-2 #10):
      * Field layout — wizards decide MudGrid / table / flex / charts /
        custom panes inside ChildContent. WizardSection does NOT wrap
        ChildContent in MudGrid.

    DoD §6 anti-layout-coupling check: this file contains zero
    MudGrid constructs.

    Reference: docs/sessions/2026-05-21-m2d1-shared-primitives-plan-v2.md §5.2
*@

@* The heading keeps its exact "{Index}. {Title}" text — that format is a tested
   contract (WizardSectionTests.Render_NumberedTitle_FormatsAsIndexDotSpaceTitle).
   The number is merely WRAPPED so it can be tinted; the text content, and so the
   accessible name, is unchanged. Spacing moved from utility classes to
   .wizard-section__head, which also draws the rule separating the heading from
   the fields — the panel previously ran heading straight into inputs with
   nothing marking where the section began.
   The inline font-weight:500 is gone deliberately: the weight-scale normaliser in
   site.css rewrites stray 500s to 400, so that inline rule was making the heading
   render LIGHTER than body emphasis. .wizard-section__title carries the weight. *@
<MudPaper Elevation="1" Class="pa-4 mb-4 wizard-section" data-testid="wizard-section">
    <div class="wizard-section__head">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="wizard-section__title"
                 data-testid="wizard-section-title"><span class="wizard-section__index">@Index.</span> @Title</MudText>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Description))
        {
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="wizard-section__desc" data-testid="wizard-section-description">@Description</MudText>
        }
    </div>
    @ChildContent
</MudPaper>

@code {
    /// <summary>Section number rendered as the title prefix (e.g. <c>1. Identity</c>).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Index { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Section title text.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional help text rendered as a small caption directly below the
    /// numbered title. When null or empty, no caption is rendered.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Description { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The section body. Wizards decide the inner layout (MudGrid for
    /// field grids, plain markup for tables, panes, charts, etc.).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
